### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/CourseManagement

### 1) GET Return the full list of students.
GET {{baseUrl}}/students
Accept: application/json

### 2) POST Create a new student (Valid).
POST {{baseUrl}}/students
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "age": 22,
  "major": "Computer Science"
}

### 3) POST Create a new student (Invalid - Age < 18).
POST {{baseUrl}}/students
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "John Smith",
  "age": 16,
  "major": "Mathematics"
}

### 4) POST Create a new student (Invalid - Empty Name).
POST {{baseUrl}}/students
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "age": 20,
  "major": "Physics"
}

### 5) GET Return a specific student.
# Assuming student ID 1 exists after earlier steps
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/1
Accept: application/json

### 6) PUT Update a student.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/students/1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe Updated",
  "age": 23,
  "major": "Software Engineering"
}

### 7) GET Search students by name (case-insensitive).
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/search?name=jane
Accept: application/json

### 8) GET Return a paginated list of students.
GET {{baseUrl}}/students/pagination?page=1&limit=5
Accept: application/json

### 9) DELETE Delete a student.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/students/1
Accept: application/json
